{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":528110,"num_turns":17,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3515f678-f21b-4d8d-a2ad-248a02d403e5","total_cost_usd":3.0139830000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":31,"cache_creation_input_tokens":112239,"cache_read_input_tokens":1614184,"output_tokens":42060,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":112239,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7688,"cache_read_input_tokens":126607,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":32746,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.032846,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":31,"outputTokens":42060,"cacheReadInputTokens":1614184,"cacheCreationInputTokens":112239,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.9811370000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"economy-balancer\",\n  \"flight\": {\n    \"dry_mass_kg\": 1200,\n    \"staged_mass_kg\": 1200,\n    \"fuel_capacity_kg\": 1400,\n    \"thrust_n\": 34000,\n    \"fuel_burn_kgs\": 10.0,\n    \"rcs_thrust_n\": 1600,\n    \"rcs_fuel_burn_kgs\": 0.5,\n    \"rotation_rate_degs\": 75\n  },\n  \"cargo\": {\n    \"base_slots\": 6,\n    \"compactor_tier\": 1\n  },\n  \"reentry\": {\n    \"heat_capacity\": 100,\n    \"heat_dissipation_s\": 5,\n    \"cargo_damage_interval_s\": 3,\n    \"unstaged_heat_multiplier\": 3.0,\n    \"off_retrograde_penalty\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"ablation\": {\n    \"cycle_toll_base_pct\": 2.6,\n    \"cycle_toll_growth\": 1.5,\n    \"heat_cost_coefficient\": 0.00035,\n    \"heat_cost_exponent\": 2.4,\n    \"skim_peak\": 22,\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier\": [1.0, 0.84, 0.72, 0.68],\n    \"heat_index\": { \"suborbital\": 76, \"low\": 100, \"high\": 146 },\n    \"cost_curve\": {\n      \"suborbital\": [14.03, 14.6, 18.71, 27.4],\n      \"low\": [24.68, 21.62, 23.56, 31.63],\n      \"high\": [57.37, 43.12, 38.41, 44.58]\n    },\n    \"plate_capacity_pct\": 100,\n    \"optimal_skims\": { \"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2 }\n  },\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"soft_landing_ms\": 5.0,\n    \"damage_per_ms_over\": 6.0,\n    \"no_gear_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"fragile_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"parachute_drag_coefficient\": 1.85,\n    \"parachute_area_m2\": 550,\n    \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms\": 4.3\n  },\n  \"tow_fee\": {\n    \"free_radius_m\": 1200,\n    \"max_fee_fraction\": 0.5,\n    \"curve\": \"linear\"\n  },\n  \"eva\": {\n    \"suit_mass_kg\": 130,\n    \"jetpack_thrust_n\": 520,\n    \"jetpack_fuel_kg\": 28,\n    \"jetpack_burn_kgs\": 0.45,\n    \"base_tether_slots\": 2,\n    \"magnet_hold_force_n\": 900,\n    \"magnet_range_screens\": 0.125,\n    \"latch_jerk_coefficient\": 0.5,\n    \"swing_jerk_coefficient\": 0.6\n  },\n  \"economy\": {\n    \"launch_cost\": 125,\n    \"replate_cost_per_pct\": 3,\n    \"repair_cost_per_pct\": 5,\n    \"band_value_multiplier\": { \"suborbital\": 1.0, \"low\": 2.4, \"high\": 5.5 },\n    \"size_class_base_value\": { \"small\": 50, \"medium\": 110, \"oversized\": 380 },\n    \"fragile_value_premium\": 4.0\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 380, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 1900 },\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1050, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 2400 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 420, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 42000 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1200, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 52000 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 560, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 8 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1500, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 10 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 480, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 130 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1350, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 170 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 520, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 700 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1450, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 880 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 320, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 1400 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 900, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 2000 }\n  ],\n  \"balance_notes\": [\n    \"FIX 1 of 2, full-hold mass re-derived from the catalog rather than assumed (audit finding no_target_moved, item 1). Summing the shipping slice — every hand-tetherable piece in the suborbital and low bands — against spawn_weight gives 39475 kg over 205 crushed slots = 192.6 kg per crushed slot; the audit's figure is 191.65, and the two agree to 0.5%. I take the audit's 1149.9 kg as the stated input and round to 1150 kg for a 6-slot hold. The previous pass reasoned from 806 kg because it averaged the suborbital band alone (134.4 kg/slot), which is the low-band half of the shipping slice simply left out. Every landing, heat and beta figure below is computed against 1150 kg, not against 806.\",\n    \"Full-hold mass doubling (GDD 2.3.5): dry_mass_kg = 1200 against a 1150 kg full hold gives 2350 kg loaded, 1.958x empty — the 'roughly doubles' claim to within 2.1%, and the previous pass's 2.35x error is closed by moving the ship rather than by re-reading the catalog. Stated conservatively, this is the compactor-tier-3 ceiling: at the shipping slice's compactor_tier = 1 the mediums ride uncrushed, so the same 6 slots carry only 120.7 kg/slot = 724 kg and the slice actually flies at 1.60x. I balance against the heavier 1150 kg figure throughout because that is the case that can fail, and because it is the number the audit named.\",\n    \"FIX 2 of 2, parachute descent speed is now an output of a stated model, not an input (audit findings parachute_full_hold_soft_landing and no_target_moved item 2). landing.parachute_area_m2 = 550 is now in the file, so rho0*Cd*A = 1.0 * 1.85 * 550 = 1017.5 m^2 is readable rather than back-solved. Terminal velocity v = sqrt(2mg/(rho0*Cd*A)) at m = 1200 + 1149.9 = 2349.9 kg and g = 4.0 gives sqrt(18799.2/1017.5) = sqrt(18.477) = 4.298 m/s, so descent_speed_full_hold_ms = 4.3 is what the model produces. Flying it in the crew's own simulator returns 4.299 m/s with the `inferred` list empty — the simulator no longer has to solve for a canopy area, so the confirmation is independent this time rather than circular.\",\n    \"Parachute margin, the thing the previous pass had none of (GDD 2.3.2): 4.30 m/s sits 0.70 m/s (14%) under the 5 m/s soft line and comfortably over the 3.5 m/s floor that keeps the Parachute upgrade meaningful. The line is crossed at m = 25*1017.5/8 = 3179.7 kg, i.e. 1979.7 kg of cargo — 72% heavier than the mean full hold. Even the densest legal 6-slot shipping-slice haul, six reaction_wheel_housing at 300 kg each = 1800 kg, lands at sqrt(24000/1017.5) = 4.86 m/s and is still soft, so the rule cannot fail on an unlucky spawn draw. Empty is sqrt(9600/1017.5) = 3.07 m/s, so descent speed grows as the square root of mass by construction, exactly as 2.3.2 states.\",\n    \"Storage and Parachute as a natural pair (GDD 2.3.6), all at Cd 1.85 with the canopy areas the upgrades set: a low-band 6-slot hold (246.0 kg/crushed slot, 1476 kg) lands at 4.59 m/s on the base 550 m^2; Storage t2 at 10 slots raises that to 2460 kg and 5.37 m/s — hard — and Parachute t1's 700 m^2 pulls it back to 4.76. A high-band 6-slot hold (500.7 kg/slot, 3004 kg) lands at 5.75 m/s on the base chute, 5.10 on t1, and 4.55 on Parachute t2's 880 m^2. So each Storage tier pushes the landing over the line and the matching Parachute tier pulls it under, and Parachute t2 is specifically what makes a loaded high-band return survivable. That is the counterweight relationship 2.3.6 asks for, and it is why the parachute upgrade effect is the canopy area rather than the drag coefficient — area is the part Mr. Armstrong can actually swap.\",\n    \"heat_index is now derived from the same masses instead of being asserted (audit finding no_target_moved, item 3). Peak bar heat scales as entry speed cubed times the square root of ballistic coefficient, and beta scales with mass. Entry-interface speeds are the Researcher's step 7: 864 / 906 / 954 m/s, giving cube ratios 0.867 / 1.000 / 1.168 against the low band. Loaded entry masses are 1200 kg plus a full band hold at that band's spawn-weighted crushed-slot density (145.5 / 246.0 / 500.7 kg per slot), i.e. 2072.8 / 2676.3 / 4204.4 kg, giving sqrt-mass ratios 0.880 / 1.000 / 1.253. The products are 0.763 / 1.000 / 1.463, so heat_index = 76 / 100 / 146 with the low-band direct entry normalised to 100 as the charter requires. This is the beta lever the Researcher pointed at when he flagged that entry speed alone gives only 1.35x from suborbital to high; here it gives 1.92x, and the difference is the catalog's mass gradient, not a thumb on the scale.\",\n    \"Ablation optimum (charter step 3, GDD 2.3.1). With cycle_toll_base_pct 2.6 and cycle_toll_growth 1.5, the fatigue toll for k+1 cycles is 2.6, 6.50, 12.35, 21.13 for k = 0..3; each skim adds 0.00035 * 22^2.4 = 0.583; the committed entry costs 0.00035 * (heat_index * skim_heat_multiplier[k])^2.4. Evaluating the charter's model verbatim gives cost_curve suborbital [14.03, 14.60, 18.71, 27.40], low [24.68, 21.62, 23.56, 31.63], high [57.37, 43.12, 38.41, 44.58] — minima at index 0, 1 and 2, so optimal_skims is 0/1/2, the high band is inside the required 1-2, and no band exceeds it. The marginal test is what holds it in place: the second cycle's toll of 3.90 exceeds the suborbital band's first-skim saving of 3.12, so suborbital commits directly; the third cycle's 5.85 exceeds the low band's second-skim saving of 3.90 but is well under the high band's 8.35, so low stops at one skim and high takes two; the fourth cycle's 8.78 dwarfs the third-skim saving everywhere. The heat term moved with heat_index; the four ablation constants are unchanged from the pass the audit accepted.\",\n    \"Heat bar against the plate optimum (GDD 2.3.1, 'upgrades buy margin, not immunity'): a direct suborbital entry reads 76 on a base heat_capacity of 100, so the cheapest suborbital descent is also a safe one. A direct low-band entry reads exactly 100 — on the cargo-damage line — and one skim brings it to 84, which is why 1 skim is simultaneously the cheapest and the sane descent there. The high band reads 146 direct and 105 after the two skims that minimise plate cost, so it is unflyable at base gear and needs heat_shield t1 (130) to survive its own optimum; t2 (170) is what makes a careless high-band entry recoverable. The plate optimum never moves with the shield tier, only the survivability does.\",\n    \"Break-even on a lazy run (GDD 2.3.6, charter step 7): the cheapest thing in the sky is a solid suborbital small at size_class_base_value 50 * band multiplier 1.0 = 50, so launch_cost 125 is 2.5 cheap pieces — inside the charter's 'two to three'. A lazy run fills all six slots with commonest junk for 300 and pays 125 to launch plus replating at 3 per percent on a direct suborbital entry's 14.03% = 42.09, for 167.09 of cost against 300 of revenue. Net +132.91, so a run that does nothing clever still clears its own launch with room, and every skim it did not need would have cost it plate it did not have to burn.\",\n    \"Fragile premium reshapes a payout (GDD 2.3.7): fragile_value_premium 4.0 puts a Cracked Solar Array at 110 * 2.4 * 4.0 = 1056 against 264 for a solid low-band medium. Because it is never crushable it pays 4 uncrushed slots against the solid's 2 crushed, so per slot it is 264 vs 132 — twice the density, not four times, which keeps the detour a judgement rather than an obligation. A 6-slot low-band haul of solids grosses about 790; the same run carrying one intact array grosses about 1580. One piece roughly doubles the run, and losing it to a hot entry or a hard landing is felt, which is the point.\",\n    \"No shear under steady tow (charter step 6, GDD 2.3.4): steady-state cable tension is m_piece * a_astronaut, and a_astronaut = jetpack_thrust_n / (suit_mass_kg + total towed mass). Substituting, tension = 520 * m_piece / (130 + total), which is strictly below jetpack_thrust_n = 520 N for any load at all — adding a second piece lowers acceleration and therefore lowers tension on every cable, so a heavy string is sluggish rather than fragile exactly as the design says. The worst legal single case is the catalog's heaviest hand-tetherable piece, iridium_battery_stack at 1150 kg towed alone: 520 * 1150 / 1280 = 467 N. magnet_hold_force_n = 900 sits 1.9x above that and above the 520 N asymptote, so steady towing can never shear at any tether count or piece combination. Shear is left entirely to jerk: latch shear at 0.5 * m * closing speed > 900 means a 500 kg satellite_bus_frame slips above 3.6 m/s closing and a 140 kg hull panel above 12.9, and swing shear at 0.6 * m * slew rate behaves the same way. Both are inputs the player just made.\",\n    \"EVA handling (GDD 2.3.5, charter step 6): suit_mass_kg 130 with jetpack_thrust_n 520 gives 4.00 m/s^2 clean. Towing two spawn-weighted low-band mediums (461.7 kg each, 923.3 kg total) gives 520/1053.3 = 0.494 m/s^2 — an 8.1x drop, about ten seconds to build or kill 5 m/s. That is 'tugboat instead of a diver' and still steerable. jetpack_fuel_kg 28 at 0.45 kg/s is 62 s of full throttle: two or three loaded round trips, not four, so the trips-versus-control decision has a fuel clock on it.\",\n    \"Tow fee (GDD 2.3.3): fee = 0.5 * clamp((d - 1200) / (785398 - 1200), 0, 1) * haul value, where 785398 m is half the planet's circumference (pi * 250000). It is exactly zero inside free_radius_m, exactly 0.5 at the antipode, linear between, and clamped at both ends, so it can never exceed 50%, go negative, or reach savings. free_radius_m 1200 assumes the landing camera reads about 1200 m across; if the Coder's camera scale differs this is the one number that moves with it.\",\n    \"Flight budget, measured rather than asserted (charter step 1). Because dry mass had to rise to satisfy the doubling rule, tank and thruster had to follow or the ship stops flying — these are consequences of the implicated value, not free choices. Effective exhaust velocity is thrust_n / fuel_burn_kgs = 34000 / 10.0 = 3400 m/s; a base ship at 1200 + 1400 = 2600 kg carries 3400 * ln(2600/1200) = 2629 m/s and launches at TWR 34000/(2600*4.0) = 3.27 with a 140 s burn. Flown through the crew's own ascent integrator to the suborbital band midpoint (102500 m) it circularises with 136 kg of fuel left, which is 197 m/s at loaded mass against a 42 m/s deorbit burn to a 290 km periapsis. fuel_tank t1 (1900 kg) reaches the low band with 384 kg spare and t2 (2400 kg) reaches the high band with 609 kg spare, so the tank tiers gate the bands. Worth flagging: the previous pass's 850 kg / 430 kg / 18000 N config does not reach orbit in this integrator at all, so the flight block was not merely rescaled, it was made to close.\",\n    \"Ballistic coefficient, and the gap to the Researcher's assumption (audit finding no_target_moved, item 3). flight.staged_mass_kg = 1200 is now in the file, so beta is computable without knowing the simulator's convention: on the shield (Cd 1.5, A 3.5 m^2 from baseline.json) beta = 1200/5.25 = 228.6 kg/m^2 staged and empty, and 2350/5.25 = 447.6 kg/m^2 with a full hold. The Researcher assumed 267 and 533 and explicitly labelled those as guesses 'to be priced downstream'. The remaining gap is 14% and 16%, against the 39% the audit found last pass, and 228.6 is far clear of the 100 kg/m^2 floor he named as the danger line. Derivation steps 8-11 of baseline.json should be re-read against 1200/2350 kg; the multi-pass argument survives the rescale because the pass-count claim scales with beta ratios, not with absolute beta.\",\n    \"What I could not fix, stated plainly. First, base_slots stays at 6: the GDD's own walkthrough puts 'Cargo reads 4 of 6' on screen, so the slot count is the design's and every mass and value above is fitted to it rather than it being moved to make a check pass. The same goes for base_tether_slots 2, soft_landing_ms 5, both damage multipliers, max_fee_fraction 0.5, magnet_range_screens 0.125, cargo_damage_interval_s 3 and heat_dissipation_s 5. Second, the schema still has no field for the jettisoned stage's dry mass, so dry_mass_kg and staged_mass_kg are the same number and staging sheds drag configuration and shield exposure but not mass. That gives staging a 3x braking improvement (Cd 0.5 to 1.5) rather than the Researcher's 4.3x. Staging remains one-way and nothing here restores thrust after it (section 1 pillar); if the Coder wants the mass drop it needs a new field, and heat_index must then be re-measured rather than re-guessed.\"\n  ],\n  \"catalog_concerns\": [\n    \"iridium_battery_stack, mass_kg (1150) at size_class medium: it is the heaviest hand-tetherable piece authored and 8.8x the suit mass. Towing two drops EVA acceleration to 520/(130+2300) = 0.21 m/s^2, about twenty-four seconds to build 5 m/s, which is past 'noticeably heavier but still controllable'. It does not block the shipping slice because the high band is deferred, but if the high band lands, either this mass wants to come down toward 900 kg or the piece wants a Jetpack tier gating it. I note the Designer already declined a trim on latch-shear grounds; this is the towing case, not the latching case, and it is a different number.\",\n    \"High-band masses collectively, mass_kg: the band runs 500.7 kg per crushed slot spawn-weighted, so a 10-slot hold at Storage t2 is 5007 kg of cargo and 6207 kg total. Even at Parachute t2 (Cd*A = 1628 m^2) that lands at sqrt(2*6207*4/1628) = 5.52 m/s — hard, with no upgrade left to buy. The high band therefore cannot be flown at full hold and full storage without eating landing damage. I believe this is intended tension (GDD 2.3.7, 'difficulty scales with success automatically') and I have balanced to it rather than around it, but it is a catalog-driven ceiling and the Designer should confirm it is deliberate before the high band is built.\",\n    \"cracked_solar_array, mass_kg (380) against slots_uncrushed (4): after the low-band revision the archetypal fragile medium is 95 kg per slot, against 246 kg per crushed slot for the band's solids — so the piece that pays the 4x fragile premium is now by a wide margin the lightest cargo per slot in its band, and a hold full of it is the easiest low-band ride home as well as the most valuable. Fragility risk is the only counterweight left, which is enough for a decision but not for a cost, and it softens 'the valuable stuff physically fights you' precisely in the band where the shipping slice teaches it. Mass rising toward 600 kg would restore the pull without disturbing the band ordering the Designer protected.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":63558,"ttft_stream_ms":1615,"time_to_request_ms":210,"type":"result","duration_ms":531201,"uuid":"8c7f4396-0e42-47c6-9a5e-008e21555544"}
